  "module": "newton_solver_suturebot.examples.needle.example_fem_needle_insertion",
  "caption": "Simulation-time playback, close on the region 1 wound with the pad drawn translucent (--transparent-pad): an entry (green) and an exit (pink) material point are picked on the two lips, the curved needle and its planned tip path (cyan) are previewed, and the coupled MuJoCo/FEM drive turns the needle through both lips, with one pause, until its tip comes out 0.05 mm from the exit; the camera then moves in on the needle in the tissue. From 2.0 s to 4.2 s, while the needle goes through the first lip, the pad is drawn opaque (the example's See through pad switch is off) and the viewer's Show Edges option is on: the dark lines are the edges (about 1 mm) of the surface triangles of the pad's tetrahedra, which in the simulated region 1 (the middle band with the wound, 29,160 tetrahedra and 7,284 surface triangles) are the outer faces of the simulated tetrahedra themselves and around it belong to the pad at rest; the needle (its blunt end is black under its lines) and the two marker spheres show the lines of their own drawing meshes; the part of the needle inside the tissue is hidden for that time, and the lines show how fine the mesh is around the needle more than a motion: at the puncture (2.2 s to 2.4 s) the lines of the first lip beside the entry shift by one to three pixels and go back. Puncture and sliding-track forces are illustrative: no fracture, no cavity and no physiological calibration, and the tissue moves 0.17 mm at most, too little to see without the lines. Playback at 60 frames/s does not measure live FPS.",
